    "summary": "High‑energy Spectrum show with a smoking Shakedown Street and epic Other One > Morning Dew",
    "review": "April 6, 1982 at The Spectrum was one of those spring nights where everything clicked. From the opening “Cold Rain And Snow” through a tight first set, the band built relentless momentum that exploded on a scorching second set. A smoking Shakedown Street (complete with a Crazy Fingers tease) segues into Lost Sailor → Saint Of Circumstance → Terrapin Station and then launches into a monster The Other One > Morning Dew that still gives listeners goose‑bumps. Brent Mydland’s piano dances with Jerry’s lead, Phil’s bass is thunderous and funky, and the dual‑drum groove from Bill and Mickey carries the crowd to a soaring climax before a sweet “Sugar Magnolia” encore. Multiple recordings capture this fire, but the crystal‑clear matrix mix best preserves the band’s locked‑in chemistry.",
